\section{Baseline Implementation Specification}
\label{sec:baselinespec_supp}

Table~\ref{tab:s_baselinespec} fixes the operational detail of the external
routes of the main-paper benchmark, so that the comparison can be reproduced
independently of this implementation. Every entry is the value used in the
frozen campaign, which selects the \texttt{medium} grid profile; where a
profile does not name a constant, the module default shown here applies. All
constants were fixed before the reported cells were evaluated and were not
tuned per SNR, per realization, or per method. Each route draws its scene,
codes, Jones states, gains, and noise from the shared per-trial realization
of its cell, so no baseline carries a private seed.

First, each route is an
\emph{adaptation} to the common forward model, not the reference algorithm
run unmodified: none of the three references addresses a blocked-LoS,
polarimetric, common-clock geometry with $K$ oriented near-field panels, and
the adaptation column names what changed. Second, under the as-published
tier of the main paper every route is stopped at the continuous read-out or
refinement its own cited formulation prescribes, so the residual gap
measures the reliability of that formulation's own acquisition and
read-out on this scene; a refinement-matched diagnostic that additionally
grants a route the proposed method's own bounded continuous polish over
$(\bp,\Delta t)$ against the exact forward model is reported separately in
Section~\ref{sec:aspub}. Third, a route that
returns a nonfinite estimate or raises is recorded as a failure and counted
as catastrophic; no such row is discarded, and the failure counts are
archived with the per-trial records.

