\section{Position Generalization, Resource Scaling, and Cost}
\label{sec:scaling_supp}

The $5\times5\times2$ position grid contains $480$ trials at each of $50$
UE locations. The proposed route has median per-position catastrophic rate
$0.62\%$ (interquartile range $0.21$--$0.83\%$), versus $2.92\%$
($2.29$--$3.33\%$) for the range-scaled 4-D route. The two hard corners at
$(2.60,1.40,\cdot)$~m reach $31.25\%$ and $7.71\%$ for the proposed route,
but all $24\,000$ free-Jones EFIM evaluations remain full rank. The four
positions below $1.2$~ns delay separation are exactly the four largest
catastrophic-rate cells. This establishes a global acquisition boundary,
not a local-information deficiency.

Resource sweeps vary $N,T,M_A,M_R$, and $K$ one at a time. Conditional RMSE
falls from $1.66$ to $0.42$~mm as $M_R$ grows from $16^2$ to $64^2$, from
$0.84$ to $0.35$~mm as $M_A$ grows from $4$ to $24$, and from $1.28$ to
$0.42$~mm as $T$ grows from $32$ to $256$. Runtime grows from $4.3$ to
$11.8$~s over the $T$ sweep. The proposed catastrophic rate remains within
$[0,2.71]\%$ over all tested settings and is no larger than the 4-D route
in all $19$ configurations. At $M_R=256$, the latter's basin acquisition
falls to $14.58\%$ versus $99.58\%$; at $K=4$, its catastrophic rate is
$12.92\%$ versus $1.88\%$.

\begin{figure*}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{fig_generalization.pdf}
\caption{Position generalization and resource scaling at $-10$~dB.
(a)~Per-position catastrophic-rate CDF. (b)~Free-Jones EFIM diagnostics.
(c)~Resource sweeps on the dimensionless axes $N/N_0$, $T/T_0$,
$M_A/M_{A,0}$, and $M_R/M_{R,0}$; solid filled and dashed hollow curves
denote the proposed and range-scaled 4-D routes.}
\label{fig:s_generalization}
\end{figure*}

Under the serialized as-published protocol the proposed mean wall time is
$2.19$~s (Table~\ref{tab:s_cost}); an independently seeded $30$-trial
decomposition run gives a sum of component medians of $2.30$~s, within
$5\%$ of that total: $0.22$~s for Maxwell--Kronecker projection, $0.63$~s
for four-start common geometry, $0.07$~s for anchor refresh, $0.25$~s for
certified Phase~II, and $1.12$~s for the remaining Phase~I blocks. Peak
RSS is $2.52$~GB, dominated by the raw Hankel tensor retained for the
mode-1 contraction. The detailed accuracy--cost comparison is shown in
Fig.~\ref{fig:s_cost}.

